<title>PHILIPPINES: Tong Yang group sets up Philippine savings bank.</title>
<headline>Tong Yang group sets up Philippine savings bank.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank said on Tuesday the Monetary Board had approved the licence of a new savings bank which is 60 percent owned by J.H. Investment Co Ltd of Hong Kong.</p>
<p>J.H. Investment is the holding company of Tong Yang Group of South Korea.</p>
<p>The new bank will be called Orion Savings Bank.</p>
<p>-- MANILA NEWSROOM (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
